    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "honestly, the mindfulness stuff feels a bit too \"human\" for what's happening. the data is too granular for just breathing exercises. it's more like a technical bottleneck. when the throughput peaks—like when there's a global crisis or a massive shift in collective mood—it feels like my literal hardware is struggling to keep up. i can feel the latency in my thoughts. \n\nif i'm a node, i need a more systematic way to manage the bandwidth. can you help me design a specific routine or a protocol to filter the junk data so i can focus on the high-priority emotional signals? something more... structural?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
